WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.667
-Happy Friday, everybody.
Today is Friday.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.701
And that's usually when I
catch up on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:05.968
I check my inbox.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.567
I return some e-mails,
of course,

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.667
and I write out some
thank-you notes on Fridays.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.734
Yeah, I do it every --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.067
I was just --
I was just wondering.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:16.033
I'm a bit -- running
a bit behind today.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.234
I thought,
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:18.567
I'd like to write out
my weekly thank-you notes

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:19.634
right now during the show.

00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:20.634
Is that okay?

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.434
Thank you. Thank you.
Thank you very much.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:27.033
James, can I get some thank-you-
note-writing music, please?

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.200
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.868
Alright.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.467
Oh, good mood.
-Chewing gum?

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:34.667
-Yeah.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:38.767
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.667
Thank you,
Major League Baseball's

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.634
new 15-second pitch clock.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:44.667
15 seconds might not
seem that long.

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:47.200
Or, as Stormy Daniels put it,
I beg to differ.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.300
-Hey! Oh!

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.567
Indicated.
Lick it.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:56.601
-No.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:00:59.534
[ Piano plays ]

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:03.934
Thank you, Florida Atlantic's
mascot Owlsley,

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:06.367
for looking like
the world's angriest Cinnabon.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.334
[ Laughter ]
Mad.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:12.601
-[ Growls ]
-He's mad but delicious.

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.801
-He's mad but delicious.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.901
Get a six-pack.
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:19.567
-Thank you, the people who keep
their ID and credit cards

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.934
in their phone case
for saying to the world,

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:24.834
"Eh, if I lose something,
it might as well be everything."

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.334
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.934
Take it all.
Just take it all!

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:31.167
-Take it all.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.734
Well, can you call your wife?

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:35.434
-No, I can't even know if
I'm legally married anymore.

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:37.734
My wedding certificate's
in it, too.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.534
-The deed to my house.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.200
[ Piano plays ]

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.834
-Thank you, glass,

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:48.434
for being the one thing
that's worth more stained.

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:50.434
-Oh, nice.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.934
That's a thinker.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.901
Yeah, that's a thinker.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.567
-That's one of those --
You snap to that one.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.200
-That's a snapper.
-Yeah. You don't clap.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.501
You think about it,
then you go...

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.000
-Yeah, Daddio.
I grok. I grok.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.701
-Yeah. Let me do it again.
I'll finish it up again.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:05.534
Try again. Ready?
-Everybody snap.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.200
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.868
-Thank you, glass,

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:12.234
for being the one thing
that's worth more stained.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.133
[ Fingers snapping ]

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.567
[ Jazz music plays ]

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:19.000
-I can dig it.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.200
Yeah, man.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.267
He's a cool cat.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:26.000
-He's got his pen.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.000
[ Music stops ]

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.067
[ Laughs ]

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:34.901
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:38.133
-Thank you, Cinderella,
for being the beautiful story

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:40.434
of a woman
who catfishes a prince.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.701
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:47.501
-My shoe.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.000
[ Piano plays ]

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.601
-Thank you, third time
guessing a computer password,

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.200
for letting me know the feeling

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.300
of what it's like
to defuse a bomb.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.167
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.434
Yes!

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.033
We're in!

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.467
Cut the blue wire.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:10.501
[ Piano plays ]

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:13.901
Thank you, sinks with hot
and cold faucets,

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.167
for making me feel
like a water deejay.

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:18.467
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my thank-you notes.

